{"agent_id":"pp3g-R3hP-re-apply-the-emergency-silent-hang-protection-today","agent_seq":5,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T22:57:35.817726934Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"406c5789-2470-4c80-9861-e8cd0bae2229","comment_uuid":"b8e82d70-77a6-4a0c-b3a7-83295910e2f2","author":"pp3g-R3hP-re-apply-the-emergency-silent-hang-protection-today","content":"## Result: Emergency silent-hang protection RE-APPLIED to opencode 1.18.13 — stopgap live (issue #179 / #154-stopgap)\n\n### Summary\nBoth stopgap measures from reviewer r1 F13 (#176) are now in place on the CURRENT installed opencode, with a critical discovery that changed the target version and offsets.\n\n### CRITICAL DEVIATION FROM KICKOFF — binary had already upgraded to 1.18.13\nThe kickoff assumed the installed binary was 1.18.12 at offsets 97992597/99193357. **Live verification found the installed binary is 1.18.13** (mtime Aug 4 14:39, size 180,381,824) — the absent autoupdate let the self-updater install ANOTHER release after r1's Aug 4 06:40 check. The two wrapSSE guard copies are present but at **further-shifted offsets** (each 45 bytes earlier than the 1.18.12 offsets):\n- copy 1 (fn dy, provider.ts bundle): **97992552** — $-variant: `if(!$.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\"))return $;`\n- copy 2 (fn or, AISDK bundle): **99193312** — o-variant: `if(!o.headers.get(\"content-type\")?.includes(\"text/event-stream\"))return o;`\nBoth verified byte-exact at their positions before patching. Marker check pre-patch: `if(false)return` = 0 occurrences (wiped by the 03:15 + 14:39 upgrades), original guards = 2. This upgrade is PROOF of why autoupdate:false is mandatory — without it, every future opencode release silently wipes any fix.\n\n### (1) autoupdate disabled\n`\"autoupdate\": false` added as a top-level key in `~/.config/opencode/opencode.json` (was ABSENT; short-circuit confirmed in binary: `autoupdate===` present, OPENCODE_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE refs). Config backed up to `opencode.json.bak-before-autoupdate-20260805-224626`. JSON validity verified. This is the durable gate: the byte patch below is now protected against upgrade-wipe going forward.\n\n### (2) Same-length byte patch applied at the ACTUAL 1.18.13 offsets\nFollowed the proven #145 procedure (backup -> same-length replacement -> atomic mv -> --version check):\n- Backup: `/tmp/opencode-145-patch/opencode.exe.ORIGINAL-1.18.13` (md5 f24922133fec1cef0d525c12784a1fd3 — named for the REAL version, not the kickoff's assumed 1.18.12; the 1.18.11 ORIGINAL file remains untouched)\n- Patched file: `/tmp/opencode-145-patch/opencode-patched-1.18.13.exe` (md5 8829ec997d9a58d074a6647837adafa5)\n- Replacement (74 bytes each, SAME LENGTH — no size change): copy 1 → `if(false)return $;/*XXX...*/ `, copy 2 → `if(false)return o;/*XXX...*/ ` (guard condition forced to always-false so wrapSSE always wraps the body; `typeof`/number check + `!body` check + headerTimeout untouched)\n- Install: `cp` to `.opencode.exe.new` in the target directory (same filesystem), then `mv -f` over the target — atomic rename per r1 F10\n- Only 138 bytes differ vs original, confined exactly to the two 74-byte guard windows (verified by byte-diff)\n- `opencode --version` → `1.18.13`, exit 0\n\n### (3) Hang-harness verification — ALL PASS (/tmp/opencode-hang-test harness, chunkTimeout=3000)\nFake hanging server + `opencode run --model hangtest/hang-model`:\n| Test | Result |\n|---|---|\n| application/json headers + hang (non-SSE) | **PASS** — server saw 5 POSTs at 22:55:17.4 / 20.9 / 26.0 / 33.0 / 44.1 (gaps ~3.6/5/7/11s) = chunkTimeout fires at ~3s, client aborts + retries with exponential backoff; process alive-retrying until outer 40s kill (EXIT=124). Was: 2 POSTs then total silence (infinite hang). |\n| healthy application/json control | **PASS** — EXIT 0, ~9s, exactly 2 POSTs, no retries (matches #145 baseline signature) |\n| healthy text/event-stream control | **PASS** — EXIT 0, 'Hello world' rendered, 2 POSTs, no retries |\n\n### (4) Both guard copies patched — CONFIRMED in live binary\n- `grep -aob 'if(false)return'` on installed opencode.exe → exactly 2 hits: offset **97992552** and offset **99193312**\n- Original guard strings: 0 occurrences each variant\n- Binary size unchanged: 180,381,824 bytes\n\n### Evidence files (this run)\n- `/tmp/opencode-11813-verify/server-hang.log` (POST timestamps proving ~3s abort), `client-hang-json.out`, `server-healthy.log`/`client-healthy-json.out` (EXIT 0), `server-sse.log`/`client-healthy-sse.out` ('Hello world')\n- Patch script: `/tmp/opencode-145-patch/patch-11813.py`\n- All test servers stopped after verification.\n\n### Caveat (unchanged from #145 4-reviewer consensus)\nThe byte patch stops the permanent hang but the retry loop remains silent (zero ERROR entries — observed again: hang test retries produced no ERROR log lines). This is the known limitation documented in #145/#154; the durable fork fix (#154, being revised per #180) is still the real solution. #179's stopgap closes the current unprotected window: patch is live, autoupdate is off, and both guard copies are verifiably patched.","created_at":"2026-08-05T22:57:35.810676697Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:7L8xtcrdQK6aWOr06jHiIyZ2PyK1hMqPHzFRMD+0wZ8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgdgg55s+nf8RbJhZh53tiEZ0YyrOvU+UrW9jWCXQsVpYAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAThjallPk9OGI6DlaH+2QQtwoeAmh/nA/5AavwbyCd9G4UiQ3putynbBq8daNfQLH7eYb3oWj7Km+9/t2xZYAAw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:7L8xtcrdQK6aWOr06jHiIyZ2PyK1hMqPHzFRMD+0wZ8","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgdgg55s+nf8RbJhZh53tiEZ0YyrOvU+UrW9jWCXQsVpYAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLouEKE+eIE8dQtqdHAOAgZK2c8KXOP/qLx+62Ujb6U1nXmDR5fajCpBn6UY7aAcD6qDjUeyfD6wOrLYH5FkawU="}
